# Generated artifacts must arrive in the working tree exactly as their
# generator wrote them.
#
# `lib/contracts.test.ts` compares data/cities-report.md byte-for-byte against
# what `scripts/ingest-cities.mjs` would emit, which is the only thing making
# the GeoNames CC BY 4.0 attribution contract enforceable rather than
# decorative. The generators write LF. Git stores LF. But `core.autocrlf=true`
# — the Windows default, and set on this repo — rewrites text files to CRLF on
# checkout, so a FRESH CLONE ON WINDOWS failed that contract on line endings
# alone, for a reason with nothing to do with attribution. CI never saw it
# because CI is Linux.
#
# A licence guard that goes red for a spurious reason is a guard people learn
# to ignore, so pin the eol rather than relaxing the comparison.
data/*.md   text eol=lf
data/*.json text eol=lf
